## Statement refuted

For every odd root order $\ell>2$, the natural generator map
$U^{DK}_\zeta(\mathfrak{sl}_2)\to U^L_\zeta(\mathfrak{sl}_2)$ is injective.

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The asserted injectivity for all odd $\ell>2$, and the rank-one
root forms at a primitive fifth root.

[F1] The identity-on-generators comparison map is well-defined and kills
$E^\ell$ although $E^\ell$ is nonzero in its source, for each odd
$\ell>2$
([[prop-sl2-specialization-map-from-dk-to-lusztig-is-not-injective]]).

## Counterexample

1.1 The value $\ell=5$ is an odd integer greater than $2$, and a primitive fifth root satisfies the root-order hypotheses in the refuted statement. [given, F1, algebra]

2.1 Apply [F1] at $\ell=5$: the source element $E^5$ is nonzero and its image is zero. Therefore the map is not injective, contradicting the asserted universal injectivity. [given, F1, step 1.1, algebra] ∎
